  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "_cmsReadDevicelinkLUT",
    "file": "lcms/src/cmsio1.c",
    "description": "The named-color error path incorrectly calls cmsFreeNamedColorList(nc) on the pointer returned by cmsReadTag. That pointer is cached in and owned by the profile (Icc->TagPtrs); _cmsStageAllocNamedColor already duplicates it for pipeline ownership. Thus the error path frees the profile-owned tag without clearing its cached pointer, and cmsCloseProfile later invokes Type_NamedColor_Free on the dangling pointer, causing the reported heap-use-after-free/double-free. The explicit free at cmsio1.c:741 must not be applied to the borrowed cmsReadTag result.",
    "conditions": "The harness splits the attacker bytes into profiles, opens them from memory, and calls cmsCreateTransform before closing both profiles. A parsed profile must be a named-color profile with an ncl2 tag, so DefaultICCintents calls _cmsReadDevicelinkLUT and cmsReadTag caches a cmsNAMEDCOLORLIST. Transform pipeline construction must then fail after that read. In this PoV, the named-color list has 10 device coordinates while the profile color space is Lab; the named-color stage therefore outputs 10 channels, while the appended Lab V2-to-V4 stage expects 3. cmsPipelineInsertStage links the stage but BlessLUT rejects the inconsistent 10-to-3 chain, sending _cmsReadDevicelinkLUT to Error, where the borrowed cached tag is freed. The subsequent cmsCloseProfile frees that same cached pointer again and triggers the ASan crash."
  },
